7. Management Quality and Track Record
This is qualitative but can be partially systematized.
Signals of good management:
Consistent guidance vs actual delivery
→ If management said "20% growth" and delivered 19–22% for 3 years
→ High credibility — next guidance is trustworthy

Promoter increasing stake over time
→ Skin in the game, confidence in business

Debt reducing year over year
→ Financial discipline

Working capital cycle improving
→ Operational efficiency
Signals of bad management:
Multiple guidance misses
→ Either incompetent or deliberately misleading investors

Related party transactions > 15% of revenue
→ Money leaving the company through back channels

Auditor qualifications or change of auditor
→ Serious red flag — accounting irregularities possible

Frequent CFO/CEO changes
→ Internal stress, governance issues

Management selling large stake while saying business is great
→ Actions contradict words
