13. Intermarket Divergence Signals
Sometimes the most powerful signal is when two related markets diverge when they shouldn't.
The most important divergences:
Nifty making new highs but India VIX also rising
→ Rally happening with increasing fear
→ Unstable, correction likely

Bank Nifty falling but Nifty flat
→ Banks are the economy's backbone
→ If banks fall alone, broader weakness coming

Rupee strengthening but FII selling
→ Contradiction — FII buying usually strengthens rupee
→ Something else is driving rupee (RBI intervention?)
→ Don't trust the FII flow signal today

Gold AND equities both rising together
→ Unusual — normally they're inversely correlated
→ Means liquidity is flooding everything
→ Could be pre-election rally or policy surprise

Crude rising but energy stocks falling
→ Sector not believing the crude move
→ Or sector-specific bad news (margin squeeze, regulation)
→ Don't buy energy stocks just because crude is up
These divergences should generate specific alerts:
⚠ INTERMARKET DIVERGENCE DETECTED
Nifty: +1.2% | India VIX: +8%
Rally is happening with rising fear
→ Reduce long confidence by 15% today
→ Prefer shorter holding periods
→ Tighten stop losses

