16. The Smart Money Tracker
Combining multiple institutional signals into one score.
smart_money_score = weighted combination of:

FII cash market (daily)          weight: 25%
FII derivative positioning       weight: 20%
DII activity                     weight: 15%
Block deal institutions          weight: 15%
Promoter activity                weight: 15%
SLB short interest               weight: 10%
smart_money_score > 0.7  → Institutions are accumulating
smart_money_score 0.4–0.7 → Mixed institutional activity
smart_money_score < 0.4  → Institutions are distributing
This becomes one of the core inputs to the morning brief and every signal alert.

How all of this upgrades the message
With all these additional layers, the confidence score now has 10+ independent inputs instead of 5–6. Each additional independent confirming factor reduces the probability of a false signal exponentially.
Think of it like this:
One signal alone: 55% probability of working
Two confirming signals: 67%
Three confirming signals: 76%
Four confirming signals: 83%
Five confirming signals: 88%
Six+ confirming signals: 92%+
These numbers are illustrative but the principle is real. Each INDEPENDENT confirmation multiplies confidence. Not adds — multiplies. Because the probability that 6 independent signals all point the wrong direction simultaneously is vanishingly small.

