Goal: Layer a learned model on top of the rules to catch patterns humans can't see.
Month 12 — Data readiness check
Before training any model, verify:
Do you have 500+ labeled examples per signal type?
Is outcome data complete and accurate?
Is feature data clean (no lookahead bias)?
Is sample distribution reasonable (not all from one market regime)?

If yes to all → proceed to training
If no → keep collecting, don't rush
Month 12–13 — Triple barrier labeling
For each signal:
  Upper barrier: entry + 2× ATR (take profit)
  Lower barrier: entry − 1× ATR (stop loss)
  Time barrier: 15:20 IST (forced flat)

Label:
  +1 if upper barrier hit first
  −1 if lower barrier hit first
  0 if time barrier hit first

This is more honest than simple forward returns
Month 13 — First LightGBM model
For your highest-volume signal type (probably long_buildup):

Features: all 50+ columns from signal_features table
Label: triple-barrier label
Validation: CPCV (not random split — time-aware)
Metric: Deflated Sharpe (not just accuracy)

Train → validate → if beats rules baseline → deploy as secondary scorer
Month 14+ — Meta-labeling
Primary model: your rule engine (decides direction)
Secondary model: LightGBM (decides whether to take the trade)

Secondary model input: all features at signal time
Secondary model output: P(trade profitable | features)

Final confidence:
  0.60 × rule_confidence + 0.40 × model_probability

Secondary model adjusts SIZE not direction

