The one rule that governs everything
Never move to the next phase until the current phase is stable.
Stable means:

No crashes for 5 consecutive trading days
Data is consistent and accurate (spot-check 10 values manually each week)
Alerts make intuitive sense when you read them
Performance metrics for that phase are being tracked

Moving too fast is how you get a system that technically works but produces garbage outputs. Slow and stable compounds into exceptional quality.

